 "notes": {
  "seca_ald": "TAXSIM SE ALD reproduced per row by isolated wages+SE synthetic probes of the pinned binary (probe v10 identity). Statutory ALD = 0.5*(0.124*max(0,min(0.9235*se, base-wages)) + 0.029*0.9235*se); axiom matches at the bridge base 186,000 (deliberate PolicyEngine-matching bridge parameter; SSA official 2026 base is 184,500 per rulespec-us us/policies/ssa/contribution-and-benefit-base/2026). TAXSIM additionally deducts half of the sec.1401(b)(2) additional Medicare tax, which sec.164(f)(1) excludes (probe: w=0, se=810,431 -> ALD 24,759.23 = 22,291.28 statutory + 0.5*0.009*(748,433-200,000)).",
  "qbid": "TAXSIM 2026-05-21 module applies 20% of (psemp+ssemp net of its SE ALD) with no sec.199A(b)(3) wage/UBIA limitation and no H.R.1 sec.70105 $400 minimum; axiom applies the statutory phase-in (pr = clamp((TI_before_QBID - 403,500 joint / 201,750 single)/(150,000 / 75,000))) and the $400 floor. Rows where the QBI bases differ carry the dispositioned rental-in-QBI bridge convention.",
  "sec461l": "axiom leg caps aggregate business loss (negative SE net of positive rental) at the 2024-vintage 305,000/610,000; TAXSIM caps at its projected 332,389.95/664,779.90 plus net positive capital gain (established empirically: psemp-only probes allow exactly 332,389.95 at any loss size; adding net capital gain raises the allowance dollar-for-dollar).",
  "ss_scope": "TAXSIM projection sums gssi over head+spouse only (adapters/taxsim/projection.py earners); the axiom projection sums social security benefits over all unit members. Member = 0.85*(benefits_all - gssi).",
  "senior": "H.R.1 sec.70103 additional senior deduction phases out per eligible senior at 6% of MAGI over the threshold; the AGI members above shift MAGI, producing the knock-on member.",
  "amt": "axiom AMT reproduces exactly as max(0, PartIII_TMT - (sec.1(h)+sec.1(j) regular tax)) from its own audited worksheet on every row; the bridge Part III grants the capital-gain stack the full 0%/15% brackets (the dispositioned capgains-worksheet-bucket-routing convention), while TAXSIM v27 carries its pre-OBBBA AMT parameter vintage (the dispositioned taxsim-2026-amt-parameter-vintage class)."
